# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# Nothing here may suppress a leak in our own code. The one entry is a
# third-party allocation made before main() runs:
#
# libp11-kit's ELF constructor calls __newlocale, which never frees its argz
# buffer. It is reached through the dynamic loader merely by LINKING against
# libcurl -- an empty `int main(void){return 0;}` reproduces it with no curl
# call at all. Without this, every sanitizer test binary exits 1 regardless of
# whether its assertions passed.
leak:libp11-kit
